  "summary": "Stops monitoring socket exception sets in select() on non-Windows platforms, and disconnects established peers if an exception triggers on Windows. This prevents TCP urgent data or out-of-band pointers from repeatedly waking select() without readable data.",
  "problem": "On POSIX systems, incoming TCP urgent data triggers select()'s exception set, which can cause the network event loop to spin continuously when no regular data is available to read. Windows requires monitoring the exception set for non-blocking connect failures, but other operating systems only use it for out-of-band data.",
